{
  "id": 9,
  "slug": "deduccion-y-gerundio-infinitivo",
  "level": "C1",
  "title": "Modales de deduccion y especulacion + Gerundio vs Infinitivo",
  "lesson": {
    "intro": "Dos bloques de C1. Primero, los <strong>modales de deduccion</strong>: como decir lo seguros que estamos de algo (<em>must be, can't be, might have been...</em>). Segundo, la eleccion entre <strong>gerundio (-ing) e infinitivo con 'to'</strong>: depende del contexto (preposicion, verbo, adjetivo, proposito) y, en algunos verbos, cambia el significado.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "subtopic": "deduccion-presente",
        "heading": "1 - Deduccion en presente",
        "body": "<p>Para expresar cuanto de seguros estamos de algo <strong>ahora</strong>:</p><ul><li><code>must be</code> = casi seguro que SI (He must be tired).</li><li><code>can't be</code> = casi seguro que NO (This can't be right).</li><li><code>might / may / could be</code> = es posible, no estoy seguro.</li></ul><p>El contrario de <em>must be</em> es <strong>can't be</strong>, no \"mustn't be\".</p>",
        "examples": [
          "She <strong>must be</strong> at work; her coat's gone.",
          "He <strong>can't be</strong> serious.",
          "It <strong>might be</strong> a mistake.",
          "They <strong>could be</strong> stuck in traffic."
        ]
      },
      {
        "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado",
        "heading": "2 - Deduccion en pasado",
        "body": "<ul><li><code>must have</code> + participio = seguro que paso (The ground's wet - it must have rained).</li><li><code>can't / couldn't have</code> + participio = seguro que no paso (She can't have seen us).</li><li><code>might / may / could have</code> + participio = quiza paso.</li></ul><p>Ojo: <em>must have done</em> (deduccion) &ne; <em>should have done</em> (critica o consejo sobre el pasado).</p>",
        "examples": [
          "He <strong>must have left</strong> early.",
          "They <strong>can't have finished</strong> already.",
          "She <strong>might have forgotten</strong>.",
          "Someone <strong>must have eaten</strong> the cake."
        ]
      },
      {
        "subtopic": "modales-continuo",
        "heading": "3 - Modales + -ing (progresivo)",
        "body": "<ul><li><code>modal + be + -ing</code> = deduccion sobre algo <strong>en curso ahora</strong>: They <strong>must be joking</strong>; He <strong>can't be sleeping</strong> at noon.</li><li><code>modal + have been + -ing</code> = deduccion sobre algo que <strong>estaba pasando</strong> en el pasado: She <strong>must have been working</strong> all night.</li></ul>",
        "examples": [
          "Listen - they <strong>must be arguing</strong>.",
          "The engine's warm; he <strong>must have been driving</strong>.",
          "She's exhausted; she <strong>must have been working</strong> all night."
        ]
      },
      {
        "subtopic": "gerundio-usos",
        "heading": "4 - Gerundio (-ing): usos",
        "body": "<ul><li>Como <strong>sujeto</strong>: <em>Smoking is bad</em>.</li><li>Tras <strong>preposicion</strong>: interested <strong>in</strong> learning; good <strong>at</strong> cooking; after <strong>finishing</strong>.</li><li>Tras ciertos verbos: <em>enjoy, avoid, mind, suggest, keep, finish, deny, imagine, risk, practise, consider, miss</em>.</li><li>Tras expresiones: <em>look forward to, be/get used to, it's no use/good, it's (not) worth, can't help, spend time</em> (+ -ing).</li></ul>",
        "examples": [
          "<strong>Swimming</strong> is good for you.",
          "I'm interested in <strong>learning</strong> more.",
          "She avoided <strong>answering</strong> the question.",
          "I look forward to <strong>hearing</strong> from you."
        ]
      },
      {
        "subtopic": "infinitivo-usos",
        "heading": "5 - Infinitivo con 'to': usos",
        "body": "<ul><li>Tras ciertos verbos: <em>want, hope, decide, offer, refuse, manage, afford, agree, promise, learn, plan, expect, seem, tend, choose</em>.</li><li>Tras <strong>adjetivos</strong>: <em>easy to do, happy to help</em>.</li><li>Para expresar <strong>proposito</strong>: <em>I came here to see you</em>.</li><li>Con <em>too / enough</em>: <em>too tired to walk; old enough to drive</em>.</li></ul>",
        "examples": [
          "She decided <strong>to accept</strong> the job.",
          "It was hard <strong>to accept</strong> the truth.",
          "I went to the shop <strong>to buy</strong> milk.",
          "He's not old enough <strong>to drive</strong>."
        ]
      },
      {
        "subtopic": "verbos-cambio-significado",
        "heading": "6 - Verbos que cambian de significado",
        "body": "<ul><li><em>stop <strong>-ing</strong></em> (dejar de) / <em>stop <strong>to</strong></em> (parar para).</li><li><em>remember <strong>-ing</strong></em> (recordar algo hecho) / <em>remember <strong>to</strong></em> (acordarse de hacer).</li><li><em>forget <strong>-ing</strong></em> (olvidar una experiencia) / <em>forget <strong>to</strong></em> (olvidarse de hacer).</li><li><em>regret <strong>-ing</strong></em> (arrepentirse de) / <em>regret <strong>to</strong> inform</em> (lamentar comunicar).</li><li><em>try <strong>-ing</strong></em> (probar a) / <em>try <strong>to</strong></em> (esforzarse por).</li><li><em>mean <strong>-ing</strong></em> (implicar) / <em>mean <strong>to</strong></em> (tener la intencion de).</li></ul>",
        "examples": [
          "I stopped <strong>smoking</strong>. (lo deje) / I stopped <strong>to smoke</strong>. (pare para fumar)",
          "Remember <strong>to lock</strong> the door. / I remember <strong>locking</strong> it.",
          "Try <strong>adding</strong> salt. / She tried <strong>to open</strong> the jar."
        ]
      },
      {
        "subtopic": "verbo-objeto-infinitivo",
        "heading": "7 - Verbo + objeto + infinitivo",
        "body": "<ul><li><em>want / ask / tell / expect / would like / warn</em> + objeto + <code>to</code> + infinitivo: <em>I want you <strong>to stay</strong></em>.</li><li><em>make / let</em> + objeto + infinitivo <strong>sin 'to'</strong>: <em>She made me <strong>wait</strong>; Let me <strong>go</strong></em>.</li><li><em>help</em> + objeto + <code>(to)</code> infinitivo (las dos valen).</li></ul><p>En <strong>pasiva</strong>, <em>make</em> recupera el 'to': <em>He was made <strong>to wait</strong></em>.</p>",
        "examples": [
          "I want you <strong>to stay</strong>.",
          "They made me <strong>do</strong> it again.",
          "My parents let me <strong>stay</strong> out late.",
          "He helped me <strong>(to) carry</strong> the boxes."
        ]
      },
      {
        "subtopic": "contraste-ing-to",
        "heading": "8 - Elegir -ing o 'to' infinitivo",
        "body": "<p>Regla rapida:</p><ul><li>Tras <strong>preposicion</strong> &rarr; -ing.</li><li>Tras verbos de gustar / evitar / terminar / sugerir &rarr; -ing.</li><li>Tras verbos de querer / decidir / planear / prometer &rarr; to.</li><li>Como <strong>sujeto</strong> &rarr; -ing. Para <strong>proposito</strong> &rarr; to.</li></ul><p>Y memoriza los verbos que cambian de sentido.</p>",
        "examples": [
          "He suggested <strong>taking</strong> a taxi. / He offered <strong>to call</strong> a taxi.",
          "It's not worth <strong>arguing</strong>. / I can't wait <strong>to see</strong> you.",
          "She's good at <strong>solving</strong> problems."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "contrast": {
      "title": "-ing o 'to' infinitivo?",
      "headers": ["Contexto", "Forma", "Ejemplo"],
      "rows": [
        ["Sujeto de la frase", "-ing", "<strong>Reading</strong> relaxes me."],
        ["Tras preposicion", "-ing", "good at <strong>drawing</strong>"],
        ["Tras enjoy, avoid, mind, suggest, finish...", "-ing", "I avoid <strong>driving</strong> at night."],
        ["Tras want, hope, decide, offer, refuse...", "to + inf.", "She decided <strong>to leave</strong>."],
        ["Tras adjetivo / too / enough", "to + inf.", "too late <strong>to call</strong>"],
        ["Proposito", "to + inf.", "I went out <strong>to buy</strong> bread."],
        ["make / let + objeto", "infinitivo sin 'to'", "They made me <strong>wait</strong>."]
      ]
    },
    "mistakes": [
      "NO: This <em>mustn't</em> be right. (deduccion)  ->  SI: This <strong>can't</strong> be right.",
      "NO: He <em>must had</em> left.  ->  SI: He <strong>must have</strong> left.",
      "NO: I'm interested in <em>to learn</em> French.  ->  SI: I'm interested in <strong>learning</strong> French.",
      "NO: She wants <em>that I stay</em>.  ->  SI: She wants <strong>me to stay</strong>.",
      "NO: They made me <em>to wait</em>.  ->  SI: They made me <strong>wait</strong>.",
      "NO: I look forward to <em>hear</em> from you.  ->  SI: ... to <strong>hearing</strong> from you.",
      "NO: <em>should have done</em> = deduccion.  ->  Cuidado: <strong>must have done</strong> = deduccion; <strong>should have done</strong> = critica/consejo."
    ],
    "sources": [
      { "label": "British Council LearnEnglish - Modals: deductions about the present", "url": "https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/grammar/b1-b2-grammar/modals-deductions-about-the-present" },
      { "label": "British Council LearnEnglish - Modals: deductions about the past", "url": "https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/grammar/b1-b2-grammar/modals-deductions-about-the-past" },
      { "label": "British Council LearnEnglish - Verbs followed by '-ing' or infinitive", "url": "https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/grammar/c1-grammar/verbs-followed-ing-clause-or-infinitive" },
      { "label": "Test-English - Gerunds and infinitives (B2-C1)", "url": "https://test-english.com/grammar-points/b2/gerunds-and-infinitives/" }
    ]
  },
  "questions": [
    { "id": "t9-001", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "He's got three phones. He ___ be rich.", "options": ["must", "can't", "might not"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Deduccion casi segura (positiva) -> must." },
    { "id": "t9-002", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "She ___ be at home - her car isn't here.", "options": ["can't", "must", "might"], "answer": "can't", "explanation": "Deduccion casi segura (negativa) -> can't." },
    { "id": "t9-003", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "I'm not sure, but he ___ be French.", "options": ["might", "must", "can't"], "answer": "might", "explanation": "Posibilidad, sin seguridad -> might / may / could." },
    { "id": "t9-004", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "There's no reply. They ___ be asleep.", "options": ["could", "can't", "mustn't"], "answer": "could", "explanation": "Explicacion posible -> could / might / may." },
    { "id": "t9-005", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'must' para deduccion expresa:", "options": ["casi certeza de que algo ES verdad", "obligacion", "posibilidad"], "answer": "casi certeza de que algo ES verdad", "explanation": "Deduccion fuerte positiva." },
    { "id": "t9-006", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'can't' para deduccion expresa:", "options": ["casi certeza de que algo NO es verdad", "permiso", "posibilidad debil"], "answer": "casi certeza de que algo NO es verdad", "explanation": "Deduccion fuerte negativa." },
    { "id": "t9-007", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "El contrario de 'must be' (deduccion) es:", "options": ["can't be", "mustn't be", "don't must be"], "answer": "can't be", "explanation": "En deduccion, must be <-> can't be." },
    { "id": "t9-008", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'That ___ be John - he's on holiday in Peru.'", "options": ["can't", "must", "might not"], "answer": "can't", "explanation": "Imposible -> can't." },
    { "id": "t9-009", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'It ___ be true; I read it in three papers.'", "options": ["must", "can't", "may not"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Casi seguro que si -> must." },
    { "id": "t9-010", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "gap", "prompt": "Completa: He knows everyone here. He ___ (must / be) a regular.", "accept": ["must be"], "answer": "must be", "explanation": "must + be (deduccion presente)." },
    { "id": "t9-011", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'She ___ know the answer; she's an expert.'", "options": ["must", "can't", "doesn't"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Deduccion probable -> must." },
    { "id": "t9-012", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'You ___ be joking!' (no me lo creo)", "options": ["must", "can't", "might"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "'You must be joking' es la expresion fija." },
    { "id": "t9-013", "subtopic": "deduccion-presente", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Para un nivel intermedio de certeza usamos:", "options": ["may / might / could", "must", "can't"], "answer": "may / might / could", "explanation": "Posibilidad sin compromiso." },

    { "id": "t9-014", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "The ground's wet. It ___ rained.", "options": ["must have", "can't have", "might not have"], "answer": "must have", "explanation": "Seguro que paso -> must have + participio." },
    { "id": "t9-015", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "She ___ have seen us - she wasn't there.", "options": ["can't", "must", "might"], "answer": "can't", "explanation": "Seguro que no paso -> can't have + participio." },
    { "id": "t9-016", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "He didn't answer. He ___ have been busy.", "options": ["might", "must", "can't"], "answer": "might", "explanation": "Explicacion posible -> might have + participio." },
    { "id": "t9-017", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Deduccion pasada (seguro que paso) =", "options": ["must have + participio", "can't have + participio", "should have + participio"], "answer": "must have + participio", "explanation": "must have done." },
    { "id": "t9-018", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Deduccion pasada (seguro que NO paso) =", "options": ["can't/couldn't have + participio", "mustn't have", "didn't have to"], "answer": "can't/couldn't have + participio", "explanation": "can't have done / couldn't have done." },
    { "id": "t9-019", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'The lights are off. They ___ have gone to bed.'", "options": ["must", "can't", "don't"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Deduccion segura -> must have." },
    { "id": "t9-020", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'You ___ have felt terrible after that news.'", "options": ["must", "can't", "might not"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Deduccion empatica -> must have." },
    { "id": "t9-021", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "gap", "prompt": "Completa: The cake's gone. Someone ___ (must / eat) it.", "accept": ["must have eaten"], "answer": "must have eaten", "explanation": "must have + participio (eaten)." },
    { "id": "t9-022", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'He passed without studying? He ___ have cheated.'", "options": ["must", "can't", "should"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Sospecha fuerte -> must have." },
    { "id": "t9-023", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'She ___ have got my message; her phone was off all day.'", "options": ["can't", "must", "might"], "answer": "can't", "explanation": "Imposible -> can't have + participio." },
    { "id": "t9-024", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'I ___ have left my keys at the office - they're not here.'", "options": ["must", "can't", "shouldn't"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Conclusion logica -> must have." },
    { "id": "t9-025", "subtopic": "deduccion-pasado", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Diferencia entre 'must have done' y 'should have done':", "options": ["'must have' = deduccion; 'should have' = critica/consejo sobre el pasado", "son iguales", "'should have' es mas seguro"], "answer": "'must have' = deduccion; 'should have' = critica/consejo sobre el pasado", "explanation": "No confundir deduccion con reproche." },

    { "id": "t9-026", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Listen! Someone's shouting. They ___ be arguing.", "options": ["must", "can't", "don't"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Deduccion sobre algo en curso -> must be + -ing." },
    { "id": "t9-027", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "He looks awful. He ___ be feeling well.", "options": ["can't", "must", "might"], "answer": "can't", "explanation": "Deduccion negativa sobre el momento -> can't be + -ing." },
    { "id": "t9-028", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "She called at 3 a.m.? She ___ have been dreaming.", "options": ["must", "can't", "should"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Deduccion sobre accion pasada en curso -> must have been + -ing." },
    { "id": "t9-029", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "modal + be + -ing describe:", "options": ["una deduccion sobre algo que pasa AHORA", "una deduccion pasada", "una obligacion"], "answer": "una deduccion sobre algo que pasa AHORA", "explanation": "must/can't/might be + -ing." },
    { "id": "t9-030", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "modal + have been + -ing describe:", "options": ["una deduccion sobre una accion en curso en el pasado", "un habito presente", "un plan futuro"], "answer": "una deduccion sobre una accion en curso en el pasado", "explanation": "must have been working, etc." },
    { "id": "t9-031", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'You ___ be joking.'", "options": ["must", "can't", "should"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Expresion fija: 'You must be joking'." },
    { "id": "t9-032", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'The engine's still warm. He ___ have been driving recently.'", "options": ["must", "can't", "shouldn't"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Evidencia -> must have been + -ing." },
    { "id": "t9-033", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'She's exhausted. She ___ have been working all night.'", "options": ["must", "can't", "shouldn't"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Deduccion fuerte -> must have been + -ing." },
    { "id": "t9-034", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'He ___ be studying now - the library closed hours ago.'", "options": ["can't", "must", "might"], "answer": "can't", "explanation": "Imposible ahora -> can't be + -ing." },
    { "id": "t9-035", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'They ___ be having dinner; it's only 5 p.m.'", "options": ["can't", "must", "should"], "answer": "can't", "explanation": "Improbable -> can't be + -ing." },
    { "id": "t9-036", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "'I keep sneezing. I ___ be getting a cold.'", "options": ["must", "can't", "don't"], "answer": "must", "explanation": "Deduccion sobre proceso en curso -> must be + -ing." },
    { "id": "t9-037", "subtopic": "modales-continuo", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Elige la deduccion continua correcta:", "options": ["He must be joking.", "He must joking.", "He must to be joking."], "answer": "He must be joking.", "explanation": "modal + be + -ing (sin 'to', con 'be')." },

    { "id": "t9-038", "subtopic": "gerundio-usos", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "___ is good for your health.", "options": ["Swimming", "To swim", "Swim"], "answer": "Swimming", "explanation": "Gerundio como sujeto de la frase." },
